  "task_retrieval_key": "A 14-year-old female presented with a two-month history of itchy skin lesions located on the upper and lower extremities, thighs, and pubic area. Her system review did not reveal any other complaints or associated symptoms. Physical examination showed well-demarcated annular brownish plaques, measuring between 5cm and 7cm. The borders of these plaques were scaly and elevated, with a few pustules observed on the upper and lower extremities, thighs, and pubic area. Some lesions exhibited central clearing. There were no abnormalities noted in the hair, nails, mucosal, or genital areas. The patient was treated with terbinafine 250 mg tablets and topical miconazole cream applied twice daily for two weeks. Upon follow-up after two weeks, additional lesions were observed on the lower extremity and inner thigh, despite adherence to the prescribed treatment.\nnan",
